# The built binary. `make build` puts it here and `make tape` puts it on PATH
# ahead of anything installed, so a recording captures the working tree.
/bin/

# Where `make tape` records. These are working files: one gif per tape plus
# every still it takes, regenerated on any run and never identical twice, since
# a live chart does not render the same way at two different moments.
#
# The frames that make up the visual changelog live in design/ and are checked
# in. `make artifacts` is what promotes them across, deliberately as a separate
# command - see PLAN.md §6.
/vhs/out/

.DS_Store
